  "summary": "A typical USB Type-C plug: a 24-pin reversible metal shell about 8.3 mm by 2.5 mm that seats 6.2 mm into the receptacle. A plastic tongue carries two rows of twelve contacts, a steel midplate, EMI springs and two side latches. The overmold holds a small PCB, an eMarker chip that reports cable current and speed, and the cable braid.",
